# The README demo: the "area of a circle" board (examples/area.lawh) built from an empty board
# with the README quick start's keys, then jump labels, `:sym` and `:export`.
# Format: demo/README.md. Render: demo/render.sh.

# 1000x566 logical pixels at scale factor 2: frames of 2000x1132, averaged down to 1000x566 by
# render.sh. The view holds the whole final board, so it never follows the cursor (the driver
# fails if it would).
window 1000 566 2
view 3.25 -0.9 1.3333
file area.lawh

pace 85
wait 1000

scene Type text where the cursor is
keys 5k
wait 350
keys i
wait 250
keys Area of a circle
wait 400
keys <Esc>
wait 900

scene Draw shapes with : commands
keys 5j
wait 350
keys :ci 3
wait 350
keys <CR>
wait 600
keys :li 3 0
wait 350
keys <CR>
wait 600
keys lk
wait 250
keys ir
wait 300
keys <Esc>
wait 900

scene Write math in Typst syntax
keys 4lj
wait 350
keys :ma A = pi r^2
wait 500
keys <CR>
wait 1300

scene Jump to any object with s, then make the title bigger
keys s
wait 1200
# `f` labels the title here (LAWH_DEMO_TRACE=1 shows each label).
keys f
wait 500
keys <C-a>
wait 300
keys <C-a>
wait 1000

scene Find math symbols by name
keys s
wait 900
# From the title, `f` labels the formula.
keys f
wait 500
keys o
wait 250
keys r = 3<Space>
wait 300
keys <C-k>
wait 450
pace 140
keys arr
wait 800
keys .r.d
wait 700
pace 380
keys <Tab><Tab>
wait 600
pace 85
keys <CR>
wait 400
keys <Space>A<Space>
keys <C-k>
wait 300
pace 140
keys appr
wait 600
pace 85
keys <CR>
wait 300
keys <Space>28.3
wait 350
keys <Esc>
wait 1200

scene Export to SVG, PNG or PDF
keys :exp area.pdf
wait 450
keys <CR>
wait 2500
